{
  // The specs are excluded from the tier's own `tsconfig.json`: they are not
  // compiled into `dist` and never were. Excluded from every project, though, an
  // editor walking up from one finds only the config that excludes it, and
  // reports `Cannot find module 'bun:test'` on the first line of all 347 of
  // them.
  //
  // This is that project, and the package `references` it so an editor is told
  // where these files belong rather than having to find a config that is not one
  // of their ancestors. Same shape as `.preview`, which does this for the
  // examples, and the same two constraints: `composite` is what a reference
  // requires and it rules out `noEmit` (TS6304), so it emits declarations nobody
  // reads into `.tsbuild`, which is gitignored.
  //
  // **`types` is named rather than left to discovery.** `bun:test` is an ambient
  // `declare module` inside `bun-types`, reached through `@types/bun`, and it
  // arrives only when the package is in `types`. Measured: without this line the
  // module is unresolved and every callback parameter in the file is an implicit
  // `any` behind it.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "composite": true,
    "declaration": true,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "emitDeclarationOnly": true,
    "outDir": ".tsbuild",
    "rootDir": "src",
    "types": ["bun"]
  },
  "exclude": [],
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "include": ["src/**/*"]
}
